course: dictionary
lesson: 15123
title: Sandbag: a bag, a wall and a trick
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sandbag is a bag filled with sand. When a river rises, people stack sandbags to make a wall that keeps the floodwater out. Context helps you here: the words flood and stacked show you the bag is used for protection.
explain: «Before the flood came, the villagers filled sandbags and piled them in front of their doors.» Filled, piled and flood all point to a bag with sand inside, used as a barrier against water.
explain: Sandbag can also be a verb. «The town sandbagged the riverbank to keep the water back.» Here sandbagged means protected the place with sandbags.
explain: In games, sandbag is an informal word with a sneaky meaning. «Maya sandbagged the first round, so everyone thought she was rubbish.» She pretended to be weaker than she was, so she could surprise them later.
fact: A sandbag is a bag filled with sand.
fact: Sandbags are used to build walls against floods.
fact: To sandbag a place means to protect it with sandbags.
fact: In games, sandbagging means pretending to be weaker than you are, so you can win later.
fact: Sandbags is the plural. The verb forms are sandbag, sandbags, sandbagged and sandbagging.
exercise: «The river was rising, so the farmers stacked sandbags against the barn wall.» What is a sandbag? | A small sack for carrying apples | A sandpit with a wooden frame | *A bag filled with sand, used as a barrier against water | A sandy beach where children play
exercise: «They sandbagged the shop before the storm.» What does sandbagged mean here? | Sold all its goods | *Protected it with sandbags | Painted it blue | Pretended it was not there
exercise: In a game, what does sandbagging mean? | Playing as fast as you can from the start | *Pretending to be weaker than you are, so you can win later | Carrying a heavy bag around the playground | Asking the referee for a rest
test: «Before the flood, the town filled sandbags and built a wall along the river.» Why did the town fill sandbags? | To make a sandpit for children | To sit on at the beach | *To keep floodwater out | To store sand for the winter
test: Which sentence uses sandbag as a noun, meaning a thing? | *«The workers piled sandbags at the door.» | «They are sandbagging the shop now.» | «The town sandbagged the river wall.» | «She sandbagged the first game.»
exam: Dev says, «I sandbagged in the quiz, so I looked bad at first.» What is Dev most likely doing? | Sleeping through the whole quiz | *Pretending to be weaker than he is, to surprise people later | Asking for help with his maths | Building a wall of sand at the beach
